# The smallest Venn program there is: text on the screen.
# Run it with: venn run examples/basics/01-hello.vn

print "Hello, Venn."

# `print` takes as many values as you like and spaces them on one line.
print "the answer is" 42 true

# Everything after a `#` is a comment, to the end of the line.
print "this line runs"   # this half of it does not

## Two hashes make a doc comment. It belongs to the declaration written under
## it, and the editor shows it when you hover the name.
fn shout(word) => "${word.upper}!"

print shout("venn")

# A file with no `flow` in it is a program: the statements run top to bottom in
# the order written, and `venn run` is what runs it. A file that contains a
# `flow` is a test, and that is what `venn test` is for. Everything in this
# folder is a program.
